WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.847
Before reading the node implementations, look at the graph shape.

00:00:03.847 --> 00:00:07.887
The graph begins at retrieve, then moves to grade.

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:11.367
From grade, there are three possible routes.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.892
Good evidence goes to generate.

00:00:13.892 --> 00:00:17.502
Weak evidence with budget remaining goes to rewrite.

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:20.832
A stop condition goes directly to end.

00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:24.762
After rewrite, execution returns to retrieve.

00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:27.495
After generate, execution ends.

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:32.754
This picture tells you most of the architecture before you read any function body.

00:00:32.754 --> 00:00:36.279
That is why I recommend drawing the topology first.

00:00:36.279 --> 00:00:40.255
It separates workflow design from implementation details.

00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:43.654
Also notice the explicit stop route.

00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:50.908
A bounded correction loop should have a normal application-level way to stop, not only a recursion-limit error.
